# Shared secret used to validate service-to-service JWTs minted by Canvas
# when it calls Daiquiri's TAP service on behalf of a logged-in user
# (issue #197 - "filter a public catalog table -> materialize as a new
# table in the user's own mydb schema"). Canvas mints a short-lived HS256
# JWT per request (target.metadata.daiquiri_auth.mint_service_token) and
# sends it as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; this side validates it in
# linea.authentication.ServiceJWTAuthentication, which only *resolves* an
# already-existing local user from the token's `sub` claim - it never
# creates one, so the same username must already exist on both sides.
# No default on purpose: a request bearing a service token fails
# explicitly (401) instead of silently trusting an unset/empty secret.
# Must be set to the exact same value as DAIQUIRI_SERVICE_JWT_SECRET in
# Canvas's own .env (the variable name differs on purpose, the value must
# match byte-for-byte). Generate with e.g.
# `python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"`.
CANVAS_SERVICE_JWT_SECRET=
